  {"clause_id": "c058", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Acreage-basis allocation of royalty on pooled production is hard to square with Paragraph 3(g)'s statement that shut-in payments \"shall not be subject to proportionate reduction\" for a well on a pooled unit. Whether the acreage fraction applies to shut-in royalty as well as production royalty is unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.20}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c059", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c060", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Saying unpooled land may be maintained \"in any manner provided in this Lease\" runs against Paragraphs 4(d) and 4(h), which terminate the lease as to all land outside a producing or drilling unit after continuous drilling ends. The two leave it doubtful whether unpooled acreage survives.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c061", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The mandatory duty to commence an offset well within 120 days is immediately qualified by \"as a reasonable and prudent operator would drill under the same or similar circumstances,\" so it is unclear whether the obligation is absolute or excused by prudent-operator judgment. The trigger distance \"within three hundred thirty feet (330') of the Leased Premises\" also does not say whether the measure runs from the well or the unit.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.32}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c062", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The presumption applies to wells producing \"within these defined distances,\" plural, although the preceding sentence states only one distance (330 feet). The plural reference leaves the presumption's reach uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.33}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c063", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Lessee shall either\" (a) pay compensatory royalties or (b) release does not say who elects, or whether the two listed remedies are exclusive of damages for breach of the offset covenant. The expressio unius reading of the enumerated remedies is squarely arguable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c064", "issues": []},
  {"clause_id": "c065", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The further-development covenant is measured only by what \"a reasonable and prudent operator would\" do, with no well count, timetable or acreage benchmark. Whether it adds anything to the implied covenant, and when it is breached, cannot be told from the words.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c066", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Requiring Lessee to conduct \"all operations hereunder at its sole cost, risk and expense\" is in tension with Paragraph 3(b), which lets Lessee net certain regulated transportation charges against royalty proceeds. Whether post-production activities are \"operations hereunder\" borne solely by Lessee is the question a royalty-deduction dispute would raise.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.27}
  ]},
